//map.geo.admin.ch/?layers=ch.bfe.statistik-wasserkraftanlagen","https://map.geo.admin.ch/?layers=ch.bafu.wasser-entnahme,ch.bafu.wasser-leitungen,ch.bafu.wasser-rueckgabe","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/TI010.pdf","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/TI025.pdf","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/TI032.pdf","https://www.ofible.ch","https://www.bulletin.ch/sites/default/files/2026-06/2026_4_Radogna_Die_Hochwasserentlastung_vor_Schwemmholz_sch%C3%BCtzen.pdf","https://hls-dhs-dss.ch/it/articles/008541/","https://m4.ti.ch/fileadmin/DT/temi/consultazione_da/documenti/risanamento_corsi-acqua_prelievi/Risanamento_deflussi_residuali_Sintesi122012_Aggiornamento022016.pdf","https://www4.ti.ch/fileadmin/POTERI/GC/allegati/rapporti/23064_7564R-magg.pdf","https://www.rsi.ch/info/ticino-grigioni-e-insubria/Deflussi-minimi-Governo-sconfessato--1789125.html","https://www.tio.ch/ticino/attualita/1576246/deflussi-risanamento-stato-consiglio-sospesa","https://map.geo.admin.ch/?layers=ch.swisstopo.swisstlm3d-gewaessernetz","https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"],"notes":"River line: official swissTLM3D (gwl CH0051440000 and CH0000550000) from the Luzzone dam (intake TI-010) down the Brenno di Luzzone and the Brenno. It passes the Sosto intake TI-025. Checked on the 1955 map at zoom 13 and zoom 15 (Castro, Biasca): it follows the old river within about 20–40 m. Near Biasca the Brenno was moved after 1955; the last c. 1 km to the Ticino differs up to about 100 m from the old course, so the line is cut at lat 46.368 (about 1 km above the confluence). Side streams with intakes (Orino, Carassino, Lucomagno) are not drawn. Water lines: BAFU 'Supply' layer for the Ofible intakes (TI-001 to TI-091, chosen by location and by the plant named in the sheets: Luzzone, Biasca). Founding year 1956 and 1956–1963 from the Ofible website (the page also contained unrelated advertising text; the facts are plausible but should be checked). Concession year 1953 from the 2019 parliament report. 436 MW/850 GWh from Bulletin 2026; the Ofible website says 400 MW and 835 GWh."},{"id":"linth-limmern","type":"hydropower","title":"Linth-Limmern hydropower scheme (Tierfehd, Linthal, Limmern pumped storage)","scale":"major","cantons":["GL"],"place":"Upper Linth valley (Glarus Süd): Limmernsee, Muttsee, Tierfehd and Linthal","built":"1957–1965 (storage scheme); 2009–2016/17 (Limmern pumped storage)","periods":[[1957,1965],[2009,2017]],"length_km":"c. 9.5 (dry stretches of the Linth and the Limmerenbach)","summary":"The Kraftwerke Linth-Limmern collect the streams at the head of the Linth valley in the Limmernsee and use the water in stations at Tierfehd and Linthal; since 2016 a 1000 MW pumped storage plant in the mountain links the Limmernsee with the Muttsee.","why":["From 1957 to 1965 the company Kraftwerke Linth-Limmern built a high-pressure storage scheme at the head of the Linth valley. The Limmern dam closed the Limmernboden (see the change on the Limmernsee). Many streams around Tierfehd were caught in tunnels.","The water drops more than 1000 m to the stations at Tierfehd and is used again at Linthal. From the compensation basin at Linthal it goes back into the Linth.","In 2005 the operator Axpo presented the project 'Linthal 2015'. Building started in 2009. The new pumped storage plant (it pumps water up when power is cheap and makes power when it is needed) lies in a cavern near the Limmern dam. It pumps water 630 m up into the Muttsee. It went into service in 2016/17."],"gained":["The stations Tierfehd (Limmern and Hintersand stages) and Linthal have together about 386 MW and an expected production of about 540 GWh per year from natural inflow.","The Limmern pumped storage plant has 1000 MW in turbine and in pump mode. It raised the power of the scheme from about 520 MW to 1520 MW and cost 2.1 billion francs.","The scheme of 1957–1965 brought about 40 jobs, tax income for Linthal and water fees for the local communities (Tagwen). Building the pumped storage plant employed well over 3000 workers."],"lost":["The Limmerenbach below the Limmern dam gets no minimum flow (0 l/s on the official intake sheet).","At the Tierfehd intake the Linth keeps 600 l/s from April to October and no water from November to March (official intake sheet). The Linth down to Linthal is a residual flow stretch.","Below Linthal the plant causes hydropeaking over 30 km down to the Walensee. From 2006 to 2011 the high flow was 16 to 32 times the low flow; a canton study says biological indicators were very probably harmed.","Pumped storage uses more electricity than it gives back: the WWF says Linthal 2015 uses 25% more power for pumping than it produces at peak times."],"before":{"lines":[{"name":"Linth from the Tierfehd intake to the return at Linthal: full natural flow before 1964; now residual flow (official intake and return points)","coords":[[46.87394,8.98144],[46.87437,8.9812],[46.87468,8.98086],[46.87502,8.98041],[46.87541,8.98019],[46.87677,8.98133],[46.8773,8.98141],[46.87782,8.98111],[46.87819,8.98063],[46.87857,8.98003],[46.8788,8.97955],[46.87911,8.97923],[46.87956,8.9793],[46.87999,8.97935],[46.88039,8.97941],[46.88084,8.97965],[46.88131,8.97986],[46.88182,8.98006],[46.88218,8.98016],[46.8826,8.98048],[46.88303,8.98084],[46.88351,8.98119],[46.88382,8.98148],[46.88426,8.98167],[46.88473,8.98172],[46.88525,8.98194],[46.8858,8.98229],[46.8862,8.98244],[46.88646,8.98288],[46.88668,8.98344],[46.887,8.98379],[46.88738,8.984],[46.88784,8.98431],[46.88816,8.98459],[46.88852,8.98488],[46.88896,8.98535],[46.88908,8.98603],[46.88908,8.98676],[46.88913,8.98731],[46.8894,8.98791],[46.89007,8.98836],[46.89051,8.98863],[46.89093,8.98882],[46.89149,8.98896],[46.89186,8.98904],[46.89226,8.9891],[46.89272,8.98896],[46.89311,8.98872],[46.89347,8.98837],[46.89381,8.98803],[46.8943,8.98756],[46.89472,8.98729],[46.89523,8.98711],[46.89585,8.98688],[46.89621,8.98664],[46.89665,8.9861