//map.geo.admin.ch/?layers=ch.bafu.wasser-entnahme,ch.bafu.wasser-leitungen,ch.bafu.wasser-rueckgabe","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/GR080.pdf","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/GR075.pdf","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/GR112.pdf","https://www.bafu-daten.ch/wasser/restwasser/data/data/er/de/GR115.pdf","https://map.geo.admin.ch/?layers=ch.swisstopo.swisstlm3d-gewaessernetz"],"notes":"After lines: BAFU residual flow map, lines of the KVR intakes (rwknr GR-062 to GR-138: Oberalp and Val Val to Curnera, Curnera to Nalps, Medel and Val Uffiern to Santa Maria, Santa Maria and side streams to Nalps, Nalps and the Sedrun intake GR-080 to Runcahez, Runcahez GR-075 onward). The BAFU line of GR-075 runs from Runcahez to Ilanz: the Tavanasa outflow goes directly on to the Ilanz plants of 1990-1992 (another company); this part is drawn as BAFU gives it. Lines are simplified. Before lines: swissTLM3D (CH0000010000 Vorderrhein, CH0007620000 Rein da Curnera, CH0035330000 Rein da Nalps, CH0005750000/CH0005750021 Rein da Medel, CH0005740000 Rein da Sumvitg) cut at official intake points: Vorderrhein from the Sedrun intake GR-080 to the Tavanasa station (26.3 km), and the side streams from the dam or intake to their mouths (Curnera 2.6 km, Nalps 4.8 km, Medel 15.6 km, Sumvitg 4.0 km). Checked by eye on the swisstopo maps of 1958 (no lakes yet) and today. Note: the map of 1961 already shows the Curnera and Nalps lakes, so 1958 is used. The side streams get water again from side brooks below the dams. The residual flow amounts are not given on the KVR sheets (fields empty), so no numbers are used.","before":{"lines":[{"name":"Vorderrhein from Sedrun to Tavanasa: full natural flow before the 1960s; now residual flow below the Sedrun intake (official intake point to the Tavanasa station)","coords":[[46.674295,8.7647],[46.674502,8.765822],[46.674579,8.766546],[46.674649,8.767267],[46.674776,8.768079],[46